# Pinned commit of github.com/mstan/snesrecomp used to build this repo.
# Bumping this is a deliberate, reviewable change (snesrecomp is a separate
# repo evolving on its own cadence). Update via:
#   git -C ./snesrecomp rev-parse dev/super-metroid > /tmp/sha && \
#     sed -i "s|^sha = .*|sha = $(cat /tmp/sha)|" snesrecomp.pin
sha = d8566c42cbcbce032076b770d5bac2b44448f6c3
# Branch: dev/super-metroid (Super Metroid bring-up is still on its own
# snesrecomp branch, not yet merged to main).
#
# d8566c4 (2026-06-08): SM bring-up — four game-agnostic generator/runtime
# changes that take this port from non-linking to executing the game loop:
#   1. variant-prune protected-set: never prune a variant directly
#      referenced by a canonical body (fixed sub_82BB7F/sub_82BBDD LNK2019).
#   2. $4212 synthetic vblank counter so the boot vblank-wait loop (polled
#      before the first NMI) terminates.
#   3. inline-argument decoder feature: auto-detect JSR/JSL routines that
#      consume inline bytes after the call (e.g. APU_UploadBankIP) and skip
#      them at every call site (no cfg hint / HLE / stub).
#   4. boot-spin watchdog: sample the recomp call stack during frame-0 boot.
